                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "BULLET PARTY is a fun, fast paced twin stick shooter with simple controls and graphics.\n\nThe simple control scheme makes the game easy to get into. WASD for moving and arrow keys for shooting direciton with 8 directional moving and shooting. The default and only shot type is triple shot which is great for shooting around corners. You are allowed to take one hit before you die on the second hit. And there's two power ups, invincibility that can destroy enemies if you run into them and quad damage that kills everything in 1 shot other than bosses. Another interesting game feature is the variable game speed. If you are completing levels without dying, the game speeds up, but if you are dying, the game speed goes down. The game's dynamic is changed to fit any player's skill level.\n\nLevels are grouped up in \"parties\", introducing a new game element each new party, that consists of 5 levels to keep the game fresh, going up to a total of 180 levels. The best thing is that levels are usually completed in under a minute, lots of fast paced action. The bad part in my opinion are the timed levels, there's a timer that forces you to maximize the damage output and do the most optimal route for defeating enemies. The other levels feature shooting behind cover and abusing your diagonal triple shot, dodging bullets and rushing to get hit while getting a power up at the start of the level to have any chance of completing it.\n\nThe graphics are very simple and not impressive, but they have decent enough visual clarity to see the enemy bullets and dodge them. There are flashing lights, but luckily they aren't very intensive to take away from the experience. For a fast paced action game like this one the music is fitting and varied.\n\nFor achievement hunters:\nComplete all 180 levels, no missables.",
